    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a clear emphasis on leveraging high-ceiling matchups against middle-of-the-road pitching. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Luis Robert Jr.** (67.58) lead the charge as our strongest plays, both benefiting significantly from favorable platoon splits and, in the case of **Sam Antonacci**, a prime leadoff spot against the hittable Bailey Ober. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (69.06) also stands out as an elite start, utilizing a substantial +15% boost from his matchup against Randy Dobnak to anchor our lineup. Meanwhile, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.15) provides our highest daily score; his position at the #3 spot and a favorable dynamic platoon advantage against Michael King make him an essential engine for our production today.\n\nWhile we are aggressive in our starters, we have monitored the bench closely, where **Liam Hicks** (38.08) and **Wade Meckler** (36.92) were the final omissions. **Liam Hicks** remained on the bubble but ultimately fell short due to the efficiency constraints of our game caps and a negative platoon outlook against the southpaw MacKenzie Gore. We also continue to manage the absence of **Andy Pages** and **Jordan Westburg**, both of whom remain sidelined on the IL. Regarding risks, nearly every slot is currently subject to \"Lineup Pending\" status, meaning we must remain vigilant for late-breaking changes. We are specifically wary of **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**, whose scores (53.94 and 56.13, respectively) are suppressed by a significant -13% SP skill penalty against Tolle; however, their massive +16% park factor keeps them firmly in the lineup for their raw power potential. We will keep a close eye on **Jackson Merrill** as he faces the daunting Gerrit Cole, though his favorable platoon dynamics should help mitigate the risk of such a high-tier opponent.",
